  "id": "DrugBank_DB00635 - MONDO_5062",
  "verbalization": "Prednisone is implicated in the development of lymphoma through a series of indirect pathways involving other drugs. The evidence suggests that Prednisone, through its indication for Chronic Beryllium Disease, leads to the use of Dexamethasone or Methylprednisolone, which in turn are associated with lymphoma. This indicates a potential mechanism where Prednisone may influence disease progression via the use of related corticosteroids. The overlapping pathways in Path 1 and Path 3 highlight a possible role of Prednisone in the context of corticosteroid use, which is a known risk factor for lymphoma. The evidence also shows that Prednisone can be linked to Lymphoma through different routes, suggesting a broader, context-dependent relationship. The integration of these pathways underscores the importance of corticosteroid use in the pathogenesis of lymphoma, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
